Bands change the ground colour for one section: compliance strips, short statements and the closing call to action.

- `aq-band--sunken` for standard tags and the documentation list. `aq-band--limestone` for one short statement. `aq-band--navy aq-closing` for the closing call to action at the end of every page.
- Put the band class on `<section class="aq-section">` and keep content inside `aq-in`.
- Text on navy uses `on-navy` and `on-navy-muted`. A primary button inside a navy band turns Limestone with navy text automatically.
- The closing band holds an `aq-h1`, one `aq-lead` sentence and one primary button. It may carry the arc motif.
- At most one navy band per page, and never two bands touching. The closing band ends with a `line-strong` hairline so it stays distinct from the navy footer below it.
